{
	"name": "Knockout Merchant",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/control/silhouette-fall-slip-prone.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>You have learned a number of incredibly dangerous tricks and those who underestimate you frequently wind up knocked in the dirt—or at least left in the dust. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><p>Your Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, or Wisdom score increases by 1, to a maximum of 20.</p></li><li><p>Your movement speeds all increase by 10 feet.</p></li><li><p>You gain an additional combat maneuver of a degree you could learn from a combat tradition available to the adept class or your archetype. You do not need to be proficient with the tradition the maneuver comes from to select it.</p></li><li><p>Your exertion pool increases by 1.</p></li><li><p>For every 20 feet you move in a straight line prior to attacking, your first melee attack of the turn does an additional 1d6 points of damage.</p></li></ul><p>Once you have taken this feat, you can no longer gain levels in non-adept classes.</p>",
